---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import { practice } from '../data/practice';

const updated = 'November 18, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | S+ Dental, Mountlake Terrace"
  fullTitle
  breadcrumb="Privacy policy"
  description="How the S+ Dental website and staff tools handle information: optional Google Analytics only with your consent, no ads, Google sign-in for staff only, and payments processed by Stripe."
>
  <PageBanner title="Privacy policy" />

  <section class="band legal-text">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p><em>Last updated {updated}</em></p>

      <p>
        This policy covers the {practice.name} website (splus.dental) and our staff tools. It does not
        cover your dental records, which are protected under federal and state health privacy law and
        described in the Notice of Privacy Practices we provide at the office.
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting our website</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use advertising or ad-tracking cookies, and we do not sell personal information. Our
        hosting provider (Google Firebase) keeps standard technical logs, such as IP address and pages
        requested, to operate and secure the site.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Website analytics (only if you agree)</h2>
      <p>
        When you first visit, we ask whether we may use Google Analytics. If you click Decline, or
        your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, Google Analytics does not load and nothing
        is sent to Google for analytics.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you click Accept, Google Analytics sets cookies and collects which pages of this site you
        view, how you arrived (for example, a search engine or a link), when you click the
        appointment button, your browser and device type, and your approximate location (city level,
        derived by Google from your IP address). Google processes this on our behalf. We see only
        totals, such as how many people visited a page; we cannot see who you are. Advertising
        features and ad personalization are turned off. We do not run analytics on the page you
        return to after paying, and appointment booking happens on Calendly's site, outside our
        analytics.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can change your choice at any time with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom
        of every page. Washington residents: see our{' '}
        <a href="/consumer-health-data">Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some pages include or link to services run by other companies, which have their own privacy
        policies: a Google Map (it loads only when you click "Show map"), appointment booking through Calendly, our Facebook page, and a
        new-patient packet stored on Google Drive.
      </p>

      <h2>Online payments</h2>
      <p>
        When we send you a payment link, the payment is handled by Stripe on Stripe's secure page. Your
        card details go directly to Stripe and never reach our systems. We receive a record of the
        payment (amount, date, and the contact details you enter) so we can apply it to your account.
        Please do not include health information in payment forms.
      </p>

      <h2>Staff sign-in</h2>
      <p>
        Our staff tools use Google sign-in. We receive only the account's name, email address, and
        whether the email is verified, and use them solely to check that the person is authorized
        practice staff. We do not access any other Google account data.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: email <a href={`mailto:${practice.email}`}>{practice.email}</a>{' '}
        or call <a href={`tel:${practice.phone.tel}`}>{practice.phone.display}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-text .narrow {
    text-align: left;
  }
  .legal-text h2 {
    margin-top: 1.6em;
  }
</style>
